      Source: StGB consolidated, half one (provenance StGB 171, 173, 174, 174a, 174b, 174c, 176, 176a, 176b, 176e, 177, with the 184h definition; German governs)
      One combined carrier for the eleven sections of half one plus the sexual-act definition. Each section is a
      SectionScope; identifiers resolve within their SectionScope. The same token (for example Person, Entrusted,
      Performs, Exploits, Care) may carry a section-specific surface form: each section's variables are declared in
      that section's own groups, exactly as emitted by the per-section build, and the per-section schemas remain the
      canonical single-section substrates. Objective Tatbestand only; intent (Vorsatz/Absicht) excluded; penalty excluded;
      silent repairs against the German recorded in the Flags annexes of the working document, not here.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Half One (§171 to §177)</Subject><Verb>commit</Verb><Article>StGB 171, 173, 174, 174a, 174b, 174c, 176, 176a, 176b, 176e, 177 (with 184h)</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBHalfOne</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>
